    "updated_at": "2026-11-12T07:59:41Z",
    "body": "Facts from #532 (the Wire Contour op) that belong to this issue:\n\n- #532 ships a **minimal** page for the kind, `crates/ui/src/egui_app/wire_page.rs`: Side and the start hole (a \"stated\" checkbox plus X / Y) on Geometry, the two workpiece planes on Heights, the Condition (a list of the ids the op's machine states) on Passes, no Feeds tab. It exists because the registry-wide tab law (`every_registry_kind_gets_its_tab_bar`) fails a kind whose tabs draw nothing. It was not designed as the final page.\n- The pane still shows the **Tool** row for a Wire Contour, which mounts no library tool (`KindInfo::mounts_tool()` is false; the op's tool is the empty word).\n- **Ribbon on a wire EDM document:** the Wire EDM section shows one cell. With an empty tool library the cell is disabled with \"No tool yet - add one\", although the kind needs none. With a tool present, the click queues a `CreateOperation` naming no tool, which the command door refuses until a condition is named (\"a Wire Contour names no EDM condition - choose one of machine ...'s conditions\"), so quick-add cannot make the op yet: it needs to pick a condition (or open a draft page first).\n- The start hole can only be typed; picking it in the viewport is not built.\n- The op's glyph and the section's glyph are the 2D contour's (no new asset).\n",
    "author_association": "OWNER",
    "pin": null,
